                                "text": "Наиболее распространенной формой этого явления в современном русском языке оказывается так называемый творительный предикативный."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "88278c55-23df-4432-b86e-70de64f1fcad",
                        "source_entry_id": "b2435ef0-137b-37c9-8481-247967e2eedb",
                        "target_lang_word": "predicative",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "predicative",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "177fa6c5-42f3-31a6-b480-91cf63558ba5",
                                        "entry_id": "b381aa12-60f5-331f-8b5f-87275c0d2dd6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Modifying a noun from within a predicate. contrasts with attributive."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b7dea9db-7626-4f2d-9a1e-abeda3639b43",
                                                "sense_id": "177fa6c5-42f3-31a6-b480-91cf63558ba5",
                                                "text": "In the sentence, ‘This house is big’, ‘big’ is predicative, whereas in ‘This is a big house’, it is attributive."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1f519401-aad0-4b12-b3a3-dcb0358286d5",
                                                "sense_id": "177fa6c5-42f3-31a6-b480-91cf63558ba5",
                                                "text": "Compound adjectives are typically hyphenated in attributive position (for example, 'a high-quality scan is a must'), whereas in predicative position, many house styles specify open styling (for example, 'this scan is high quality.'"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "predicative",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "50d4703f-1724-366c-aef6-56af9e8d14ac",
                                        "entry_id": "c8d16223-36be-336f-94b4-fa540d10ab11",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An element of the predicate of a sentence which complements the subject or object by means of the verb. Predicatives may be nominal or adjectival."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "854c4280-97c6-3706-a7aa-a5e6f6d35978",
                                        "entry_id": "c8d16223-36be-336f-94b4-fa540d10ab11",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In some languages, a special part of speech used as a predicate and denoting a state of being."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f6f1120c-8644-4435-a4b5-207db2a29164",
                                                "sense_id": "854c4280-97c6-3706-a7aa-a5e6f6d35978",
                                                "text": "A predicative in Russian is an uninflected word that regularly constitutes a complete utterance when standing alone, i.e., when preceded and followed by silence."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "12898d92-2854-4624-a2a0-d6111cf22b16",
                                                "sense_id": "854c4280-97c6-3706-a7aa-a5e6f6d35978",
                                                "text": "Traditional grammars usually differentiate between neuter short adjectives and predicatives based on whether there is an overt nominative subject; hence курение вредно ‘smoking (noun) is harmful’ is viewed as a clause with nominative subject, zero copula and neuter short form adjective that agrees with the subject in gender, whereas курить вредно (same meaning, literally ‘to smoke is harmful’) is often viewed as an impersonal clause with predicative."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
